WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.487
Module fourteen:

2
00:00:01.487 --> 00:00:04.329
taxes and rules, an overview by country.

3
00:00:04.329 --> 00:00:06.888
This is an overview, not tax advice:

4
00:00:06.888 --> 00:00:10.156
the rules change every year, so before filing,

5
00:00:10.156 --> 00:00:13.070
check with your tax office or an adviser.

6
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.512
In most countries a coin is property.

7
00:00:16.512 --> 00:00:20.340
Tax arises not when you buy, but when the coin leaves you:

8
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.858
sold, swapped or spent.

9
00:00:21.858 --> 00:00:27.006
Almost everywhere gains are taxed, swapping one coin for another is taxed too.

10
00:00:28.006 --> 00:00:31.643
The second question is how the tax office sees the profit.

11
00:00:31.643 --> 00:00:34.152
If you hold coins and sell now and then,

12
00:00:34.152 --> 00:00:38.228
it is usually a capital gain with a separate, often reduced rate.

13
00:00:38.228 --> 00:00:42.994
If trading looks like a job, with frequent trades, a bot and an aim to earn,

14
00:00:42.994 --> 00:00:46.318
the profit may be treated as income at the full rate.

15
00:00:47.318 --> 00:00:52.425
The third question is which purchase price to deduct if you bought several times.

16
00:00:52.425 --> 00:00:54.002
The method is set by law:

17
00:00:54.002 --> 00:00:57.343
in order of purchase, by average price, or otherwise.

18
00:00:57.343 --> 00:01:00.938
The method determines how much profit lands in this year.

19
00:01:00.938 --> 00:01:05.730
So for every trade keep the date, quantity, price in local currency and fee,

20
00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:08.630
and download your exchange history every year.

21
00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:14.608
Tax is paid in the country of tax residency, not in the exchange's country.

22
00:01:14.608 --> 00:01:19.254
A resident pays tax on trades on any exchange, including foreign ones.

23
00:01:20.254 --> 00:01:23.295
Ten countries and regions on five questions:

24
00:01:23.295 --> 00:01:28.824
tax on gains, coin-to-coin swaps, exchange licences, leverage and data exchange.

25
00:01:28.824 --> 00:01:34.630
Green means the rule is milder for an individual, yellow is ordinary, red is strict.

26
00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:41.195
Under CARF rules, exchanges collect client data and pass it to their own country's

27
00:01:41.195 --> 00:01:45.131
tax office, which forwards it to the country of residence.

28
00:01:45.131 --> 00:01:50.289
Tax offices will see 2026 trades on exchanges in the European Union, the UK,

29
00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:52.393
South Africa and Japan in 2027.

30
00:01:52.393 --> 00:01:55.176
The UAE and Singapore start a year later.

31
00:01:55.176 --> 00:02:00.062
“An exchange abroad” no longer means “the tax office will not find out”.

32
00:02:01.062 --> 00:02:02.338
Take South Africa.

33
00:02:02.338 --> 00:02:04.607
There is no separate crypto tax:

34
00:02:04.607 --> 00:02:10.350
profit is taxed as income or as a capital gain, and that is decided by the facts.

35
00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.186
Swapping one coin for another is barter.

36
00:02:13.186 --> 00:02:16.519
Since 2022 intermediaries need an FSCA licence,

37
00:02:16.519 --> 00:02:19.213
and CARF has applied since March 2026:

38
00:02:19.213 --> 00:02:22.758
SARS will match exchange data against your return.

39
00:02:23.758 --> 00:02:26.294
The spread between countries is wide.

40
00:02:26.294 --> 00:02:31.639
In Germany, coins sold after more than a year are not taxed for an individual.

41
00:02:31.639 --> 00:02:37.053
In the UK it is 18 or 24 percent, and the first 3,000 pounds of gains are free.

42
00:02:37.053 --> 00:02:40.891
In the UAE, Singapore and Hong Kong gains are not taxed,

43
00:02:40.891 --> 00:02:43.152
but only for their tax residents.

44
00:02:43.152 --> 00:02:47.470
In Japan it is currently up to 55 percent on the general scale.

45
00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:49.553
The main points.

46
00:02:49.553 --> 00:02:52.259
Tax is paid in the country of residency,

47
00:02:52.259 --> 00:02:55.981
and almost everywhere a coin-to-coin swap is taxed too.

48
00:02:55.981 --> 00:02:57.943
Every trade must be recorded.

49
00:02:57.943 --> 00:03:01.732
And from 2026 exchanges pass client data to tax offices.

50
00:03:01.732 --> 00:03:05.318
Details for each country are in the module's lessons.
